<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argentocoxus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 210 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Argentocoxus was a Caledonian chieftain in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> around 210 CE, known only from the history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassius-dio">Cassius Dio</a>. During peace talks after the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a>, the empress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julia-domna">Julia Domna</a> jested about the free ways of British women, and Argentocoxus's wife replied that they consorted openly with the best men, while Roman women were seduced in secret by the worst.</p></div>
